.TH ADB-AUTO 1 "November 2026" "adb-auto 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
adb-auto \- connect Googlebook Linux terminal to Android Wireless Debugging automatically
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B adb-auto
[\fB\-h\fR]
[\fB\-p\fR [\fIPIN\fR]]
[\fB\-s\fR]
[\fB\-d\fR]
[\fB\-V\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B adb-auto
connects the Debian Linux terminal on a Googlebook (Android Laptop) to the
local Android Host over Wireless Debugging without looking up IP addresses or
changing port numbers.
.PP
.B Note:
Requires \fBUse wireless debugging\fR to be turned ON in Android Settings:
.br
\fBSettings \-> System \-> Developer options \-> Wireless debugging\fR
.PP
Android automatically suspends Wireless Debugging after sleep or Wi-Fi changes
(sometimes showing \fIUnavailable\fR while the switch still looks ON). If
connection fails, toggle \fBUse wireless debugging\fR OFF and back ON, then
run \fBadb-auto\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-pair " [\fIPIN\fR]"
Pair device using 6-digit PIN (first-time setup). Automatically discovers the
Googlebook IP and pairing port. Prompts for the 6-digit PIN if not given on
the command line, then connects immediately.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-status
Show pairing state, IP addresses, and connection status.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-disconnect
Disconnect all ADB sessions.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show version and license information.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Connect automatically (when Wireless Debugging is ON):
.B adb-auto
.TP
Pair for the first time (prompts for 6-digit PIN):
.B adb-auto \-\-pair
.TP
Pair with PIN 123456 and connect immediately:
.B adb-auto \-\-pair 123456
.TP
Check pairing and connection status:
.B adb-auto \-\-status
.TP
Disconnect ADB:
.B adb-auto \-\-disconnect
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.android/adbkey, ~/.android/adb_known_hosts.pb
Standard ADB cryptographic keys and trusted host certificates created during
one-time pairing.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/adb-auto/last_wifi_ip
Cached Googlebook Wi-Fi IP address.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Connected (or already connected), paired, or completed requested command.
.TP
.B 1
Wireless Debugging is OFF/suspended, pairing failed, or Wi-Fi is disconnected.
.TP
.B 130
Cancelled by user (\fBCtrl+C\fR).
